IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `soga-buyers`

-- Sale of Goods Act 1979, ss 1, 3, 6, 7, 8, 11, 12 to 15A, 17, 18, 20, 21, 23 to 25, 30, 35, 36, 37, 49 to 51, 53, 57 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_sale-of-goods-act-1979_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `ss 1(1), 2(1), 61(1), 62(4) -- does the Act reach my purchase`

#ASSERT `Does the Sale of Goods Act apply to my purchase` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act applies`
#ASSERT `Does the Sale of Goods Act apply to my purchase` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not apply`
#ASSERT `Does the Sale of Goods Act apply to my purchase` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Act does not apply`
#ASSERT `Does the Sale of Goods Act apply to my purchase` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 1980) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: a contract made before 19 May 1985 is read with the Schedule`

§ `ss 3(2), 8 -- what price I must pay`

#ASSERT `What price must I pay` (JUST 500) 300 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `What price must I pay` NOTHING 300 EQUALS 300

#ASSERT `What must I pay for goods bought while I could not contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE 80 EQUALS (JUST 80)
#ASSERT `What must I pay for goods bought while I could not contract` FALSE TRUE TRUE 80 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `ss 6, 7 -- goods that perish`

#ASSERT `What happens to my contract when the goods perish` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `void under section 6`
#ASSERT `What happens to my contract when the goods perish` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `neither section 6 nor section 7 ends it`
#ASSERT `What happens to my contract when the goods perish` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `avoided under section 7`

§ `s 12 -- what the seller promises about title`

#ASSERT `What does the seller promise me about title` FALSE EQUALS `a condition that the seller has the right to sell, with warranties of no undisclosed charge and of quiet possession`
#ASSERT `What does the seller promise me about title` TRUE EQUALS `only warranties that known charges were disclosed and that my quiet possession will not be disturbed`

§ `ss 11(3), 13 to 15A -- the implied conditions, and whether I may reject`

