#ASSERT `What can I do about the goods` `a shop phone with a hidden fault, kept and used for months` EQUALS `I may claim damages or set the breach against the price, but not reject`
#ASSERT `What can I do about the goods` `a shop phone with a hidden fault, accepted, under a severable contract` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: a severable contract partly accepted turns on section 31(2)`
#ASSERT `What can I do about the goods` `a sole trader's printer with a slight fault` EQUALS `I may claim damages or set the breach against the price, but not reject`
#ASSERT `What can I do about the goods` `a consumer's printer with a fault shown to be slight` EQUALS `I may reject the goods and treat the contract as repudiated`
#ASSERT `What can I do about the goods` `a shop phone with a hidden fault bought in 1984` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: a contract made before 19 May 1985 is read with the Schedule`

§ `s 35 -- have I accepted the goods`

`I signed the delivery note saying I accepted, after checking the goods` MEANS `What I did with the goods` WITH
    `the goods have been delivered to me` IS TRUE
    `I told the seller I accepted them` IS TRUE
    `I did an act inconsistent with the seller's ownership` IS FALSE
    `I had examined them or had a reasonable opportunity to examine them` IS TRUE
    `I agreed to give up my chance to examine them` IS FALSE
    `the seller has shown that I do not deal as consumer` IS FALSE
    `I kept them beyond a reasonable time without telling the seller I rejected them` IS FALSE
    `I asked the seller to repair them` IS FALSE
    `I passed them on under a sub-sale` IS FALSE

`I unwrapped and used the goods the day they came, before any chance to examine` MEANS `What I did with the goods` WITH
    `the goods have been delivered to me` IS TRUE
    `I told the seller I accepted them` IS FALSE
    `I did an act inconsistent with the seller's ownership` IS TRUE
    `I had examined them or had a reasonable opportunity to examine them` IS FALSE
    `I agreed to give up my chance to examine them` IS FALSE
    `the seller has shown that I do not deal as consumer` IS FALSE
    `I kept them beyond a reasonable time without telling the seller I rejected them` IS FALSE
    `I asked the seller to repair them` IS FALSE
    `I passed them on under a sub-sale` IS FALSE

`as a consumer I signed away my chance to examine and then used them` MEANS `What I did with the goods` WITH
    `the goods have been delivered to me` IS TRUE
    `I told the seller I accepted them` IS FALSE
    `I did an act inconsistent with the seller's ownership` IS TRUE
    `I had examined them or had a reasonable opportunity to examine them` IS FALSE
    `I agreed to give up my chance to examine them` IS TRUE
    `the seller has shown that I do not deal as consumer` IS FALSE
    `I kept them beyond a reasonable time without telling the seller I rejected them` IS FALSE
    `I asked the seller to repair them` IS FALSE
    `I passed them on under a sub-sale` IS FALSE

`I only asked the seller to repair them` MEANS `What I did with the goods` WITH
    `the goods have been delivered to me` IS TRUE
    `I told the seller I accepted them` IS FALSE
    `I did an act inconsistent with the seller's ownership` IS FALSE
    `I had examined them or had a reasonable opportunity to examine them` IS TRUE
    `I agreed to give up my chance to examine them` IS FALSE
    `the seller has shown that I do not deal as consumer` IS FALSE
    `I kept them beyond a reasonable time without telling the seller I rejected them` IS FALSE
    `I asked the seller to repair them` IS TRUE
    `I passed them on under a sub-sale` IS FALSE

`I kept them for months without saying I rejected them` MEANS `What I did with the goods` WITH
    `the goods have been delivered to me` IS TRUE
    `I told the seller I accepted them` IS FALSE
    `I did an act inconsistent with the seller's ownership` IS FALSE
    `I had examined them or had a reasonable opportunity to examine them` IS FALSE
    `I agreed to give up my chance to examine them` IS FALSE
    `the seller has shown that I do not deal as consumer` IS FALSE
    `I kept them beyond a reasonable time without telling the seller I rejected them` IS TRUE
    `I asked the seller to repair them` IS FALSE
    `I passed them on under a sub-sale` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Have I accepted the goods` `I signed the delivery note saying I accepted, after checking the goods`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I accepted the goods` `I unwrapped and used the goods the day they came, before any chance to examine`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I accepted the goods` `as a consumer I signed away my chance to examine and then used them`
#ASSERT NOT `Have I accepted the goods` `I only asked the seller to repair them`
#ASSERT `Have I accepted the goods` `I kept them for months without saying I rejected them`

§ `s 36 -- rejected goods`

#ASSERT NOT `Must I return goods I have rightly rejected` FALSE

§ `ss 17, 18, 20 -- when the goods become mine, and at my risk`

`nothing further has happened` MEANS `The steps taken` WITH
    `a different intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the seller has done the thing and I have notice of it` IS FALSE
    `I signified approval or did an act adopting the transaction` IS FALSE
    `I kept the goods without notice of rejection past the fixed or a reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `goods in a deliverable state were unconditionally appropriated with assent` IS FALSE

`the seller finished the work and told me` MEANS `The steps taken` WITH
    `a different intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the seller has done the thing and I have notice of it` IS TRUE
    `I signified approval or did an act adopting the transaction` IS FALSE
    `I kept the goods without notice of rejection past the fixed or a reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `goods in a deliverable state were unconditionally appropriated with assent` IS FALSE

`I kept the dress on approval past the return date` MEANS `The steps taken` WITH
    `a different intention appears` IS FALSE
    `the seller has done the thing and I have notice of it` IS FALSE
    `I signified approval or did an act adopting the transaction` IS FALSE
    `I kept the goods without notice of rejection past the fixed or a reasonable time` IS TRUE
    `goods in a deliverable state were unconditionally appropriated with assent` IS FALSE

`we agreed it stays the seller's until I pay` MEANS `The steps taken` WITH
    `a different intention appears` IS TRUE
    `the seller has done the thing and I have notice of it` IS FALSE
    `I signified approval or did an act adopting the transaction` IS FALSE
    `I kept the goods without notice of rejection past the fixed or a reasonable time` IS FALSE
    `goods in a deliverable state were unconditionally appropriated with assent` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Have the goods become mine` `specific goods in a deliverable state, unconditionally` `nothing further has happened` EQUALS `the property has passed to me`
#ASSERT `Have the goods become mine` `specific goods the seller must still put into a deliverable state` `nothing further has happened` EQUALS `the property has not passed to me`
#ASSERT `Have the goods become mine` `specific goods the seller must still put into a deliverable state` `the seller finished the work and told me` EQUALS `the property has passed to me`
#ASSERT `Have the goods become mine` `goods on approval or on sale or return` `I kept the dress on approval past the return date` EQUALS `the property has passed to me`
#ASSERT `Have the goods become mine` `specific goods in a deliverable state, unconditionally` `we agreed it stays the seller's until I pay` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: the parties' own intention governs under section 17`

#ASSERT `Do I bear the loss of the goods` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Do I bear the loss of the goods` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
#ASSERT `Do I bear the loss of the goods` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (JUST FALSE)

§ `ss 21, 23, 24, 25 -- do I own goods bought from someone who did not`

`a bicycle bought honestly from a thief` MEANS `How I came by the goods` WITH
    `the seller owned the goods or sold with the owner's authority or consent` IS FALSE
    `the owner's conduct precludes denying the seller's authority` IS FALSE
    `the seller had a voidable title not yet avoided when I bought` IS FALSE
    `the seller had already sold them to someone else but stayed in possession` IS FALSE
    `the seller was a buyer in possession with the original seller's consent` IS FALSE
    `the goods were delivered or transferred to me` IS TRUE
    `I acted honestly and without notice of the defect, earlier sale or other right` IS TRUE

`a watch bought honestly from a fraudster who got it by a voidable deal` MEANS `How I came by the goods` WITH
    `the seller owned the goods or sold with the owner's authority or consent` IS FALSE
    `the owner's conduct precludes denying the seller's authority` IS FALSE
    `the seller had a voidable title not yet avoided when I bought` IS TRUE
    `the seller had already sold them to someone else but stayed in possession` IS FALSE
    `the seller was a buyer in possession with the original seller's consent` IS FALSE
    `the goods were delivered or transferred to me` IS TRUE
    `I acted honestly and without notice of the defect, earlier sale or other right` IS TRUE

`the same watch, knowing of the fraud` MEANS `How I came by the goods` WITH
    `the seller owned the goods or sold with the owner's authority or consent` IS FALSE
    `the owner's conduct precludes denying the seller's authority` IS FALSE
    `the seller had a voidable title not yet avoided when I bought` IS TRUE
    `the seller had already sold them to someone else but stayed in possession` IS FALSE
    `the seller was a buyer in possession with the original seller's consent` IS FALSE
    `the goods were delivered or transferred to me` IS TRUE
    `I acted honestly and without notice of the defect, earlier sale or other right` IS FALSE

`a sofa delivered to me by a shop that had already sold it to someone else` MEANS `How I came by the goods` WITH
    `the seller owned the goods or sold with the owner's authority or consent` IS FALSE
    `the owner's conduct precludes denying the seller's authority` IS FALSE
    `the seller had a voidable title not yet avoided when I bought` IS FALSE
    `the seller had already sold them to someone else but stayed in possession` IS TRUE
    `the seller was a buyer in possession with the original seller's consent` IS FALSE
    `the goods were delivered or transferred to me` IS TRUE
    `I acted honestly and without notice of the defect, earlier sale or other right` IS TRUE

`a car bought from a buyer who had it on the original seller's consent` MEANS `How I came by the goods` WITH
    `the seller owned the goods or sold with the owner's authority or consent` IS FALSE
    `the owner's conduct precludes denying the seller's authority` IS FALSE
    `the seller had a voidable title not yet avoided when I bought` IS FALSE
    `the seller had already sold them to someone else but stayed in possession` IS FALSE
    `the seller was a buyer in possession with the original seller's consent` IS TRUE
    `the goods were delivered or transferred to me` IS TRUE
    `I acted honestly and without notice of the defect, earlier sale or other right` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Do I own the goods I bought` `a bicycle bought honestly from a thief` EQUALS `I have no better title than the seller had`
#ASSERT `Do I own the goods I bought` `a watch bought honestly from a fraudster who got it by a voidable deal` EQUALS `I have a good title`
#ASSERT `Do I own the goods I bought` `the same watch, knowing of the fraud` EQUALS `I have no better title than the seller had`
#ASSERT `Do I own the goods I bought` `a sofa delivered to me by a shop that had already sold it to someone else` EQUALS `I have a good title`
#ASSERT `Do I own the goods I bought` `a car bought from a buyer who had it on the original seller's consent` EQUALS `not covered by this encoding: section 25 takes its effect from the Factors Act 1889`

